<.shell title="File drop" current={:file_drop}>
  <h1>File drop</h1>
  <p class="lead">Drop, paste, or select a file to upload.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="measure">
      <.file_drop
        id="file-drop-demo"
        upload={SampleData.sample_upload(:empty)}
        label="Certificate"
        kinds="a photo or a PDF"
      >
        A photo or a PDF, up to 10 MB.
      </.file_drop>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>A file over it</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="measure">
      <.file_drop
        id="file-drop-demo-over"
        upload={SampleData.sample_upload(:empty)}
        label="Certificate"
        kinds="a photo or a PDF"
        class="phx-drop-target-active"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>A file chosen</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="measure">
      <.file_drop
        id="file-drop-demo-chosen"
        upload={SampleData.sample_upload(:chosen)}
        label="Certificate"
        kinds="a photo or a PDF"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Refused</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="measure">
      <.file_drop
        id="file-drop-demo-refused"
        upload={SampleData.sample_upload(:too_large)}
        label="Certificate"
        kinds="a photo or a PDF"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    Every upload: a certificate, a member's photo, a signature, or a logo. One file at a time.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Drop a file on the box, or select the browser's own button.</li>
    <li>
      Paste a file anywhere on the page, such as a screenshot. It works only on a page with one file drop.
    </li>
    <li>A photo shows small once chosen, and Remove takes it off.</li>
    <li>On a phone or iPad it is the button alone, which offers the camera.</li>
    <li>What it has now, such as the current logo, shows above the box.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.file_drop upload=&#123;@uploads.x&#125; label="…" kinds="a photo or a PDF"&gt;hint&lt;/.file_drop&gt;</code>
    for an upload from <code>allow_upload/3</code>. Its Remove sends <code>cancel-upload</code>
    with the entry's ref.
  </p>
</.shell>
